    "updated_at": "2022-06-14T19:35:41Z",
    "body": "Yeah, I do think it's logical, it's just that nothing really takes advantage of it. @emilio pointed that checking `mutable` is more consistent with what `showPicker()` does, but I believe having a picker and having an activation behavior are two separate things. (Not all picker-supported types have activation behaviors and vise versa.)\r\n\r\nI'm also okay with keeping it as-is and add a note about this. (A note would still be helpful even if it becomes `disabled`.)",
